# The ClawHub publish bundle, written by scripts/publish-clawhub.cjs.
# Deliberately not committed: it is a copy of the artifact served from the live
# domain, and a committed copy would be a second source of truth that drifts
# from the one the discovery index's digest actually describes.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH ON PURPOSE. An unanchored `skills/` matches a
# directory of that name at any depth, which silently excluded app/skills,
# app/v1/skills, app/api/skills and app/well-known/skills: the entire resident
# skills feature would have been left out of every commit while looking perfectly
# healthy in the working tree. Only this one top-level bundle is generated.
/skills/

# The Claude Code marketplace bundle, written by scripts/build-claude-plugin.cjs.
# Not committed for the same reason as /skills above — it is derived from the
# artifact the live domain serves — and for one more: a marketplace must sit at
# the ROOT of its own repository for Claude Code to find it, so this directory is
# a staging area that gets copied out, never a place that is published from here.
/claude-plugin/

# Supabase CLI scratch (version marker, linked project ref)
supabase/.temp/
